WEBVTT

00:00.760 --> 00:07.140
The Losers' Revival round ended 
with Miura-san being set free.

00:04.220 --> 00:08.980
Yeah!

01:39.490 --> 01:45.500
Contraband Game

01:39.540 --> 01:43.860
The remaining eight of you 
will proceed to the third game.

01:43.860 --> 01:48.110
As this was the Losers' Revival round, 
there will be no drop-outs.

01:48.500 --> 01:52.890
Please return to this site on 
Saturday two weeks from now.

01:52.890 --> 01:55.710
Wait, we're doing the 
third game here, too?

01:55.710 --> 01:57.970
You will receive details at a later time.

01:57.970 --> 02:01.800
Best of luck to you all in the third game.

02:03.550 --> 02:06.580
Damn, the third game's that soon?

02:06.580 --> 02:09.850
Don't worry! We've got 
Nao-chan on our side!

02:09.850 --> 02:11.850
She's got our backs!

02:11.850 --> 02:13.860
Yeah, you're right.

02:14.880 --> 02:18.350
Meanwhile, my own feelings 
were far more complicated.

02:19.580 --> 02:21.070
Don't worry about it.

02:21.890 --> 02:24.540
You intended to use the money 
you won in the revival round

02:24.540 --> 02:28.080
to get me out of the game, right?

02:28.310 --> 02:30.330
H-He's sharp!

02:31.640 --> 02:34.830
I'm taking part in the game 
of my own volition.

02:35.120 --> 02:38.130
Even if you gave me the money,
I wouldn't drop out.

02:38.690 --> 02:42.160
Not until I find out who's 
behind this ridiculous game.

02:42.950 --> 02:46.100
So, why did you call me here today?

02:47.000 --> 02:50.260
The third-round game is tomorrow.

02:50.260 --> 02:53.310
I guess I'm starting to get scared.

02:53.550 --> 02:56.550
You have your surefire plan, right?

02:56.550 --> 03:00.620
"If everyone can be honest,
we'll all be saved."

03:00.620 --> 03:03.200
"That's what the Liar Game 
is really about."

03:03.200 --> 03:04.700
You said so yourself, right?

03:05.590 --> 03:09.510
I hope everyone agrees with me.

03:10.050 --> 03:10.950
But...

03:11.410 --> 03:14.980
The ever-faithful Nao is starting 
to doubt the goodness of others?

03:14.980 --> 03:17.970
That's an awful thing to think, isn't it?

03:17.970 --> 03:20.730
No, it's good to have doubts.

03:21.380 --> 03:25.600
Doubting people means trying 
to learn more about them.

03:26.290 --> 03:29.540
To trust is certainly a noble thing.

03:30.150 --> 03:35.460
But what many people actually 
do under the guise of "trust"...

03:35.910 --> 03:38.090
is forsake actually
 getting to know others.

03:39.950 --> 03:43.680
That's not trust. It's indifference.

03:44.390 --> 03:46.900
Doubting people isn't wicked.

03:47.200 --> 03:51.040
True wickedness comes from indifference.

03:51.830 --> 03:55.800
Akiyama-san's words pierced 
my heart like a knife.

03:56.610 --> 04:00.470
He'd perfectly described 
the way I'd lived up till then.

04:01.800 --> 04:05.500
I'd been convinced that 
trusting people was good

04:05.500 --> 04:09.050
and doubting them was wicked.

04:09.830 --> 04:12.990
Even if I could have friendly 
conversations on the surface,

04:12.990 --> 04:18.350
maybe I was running from getting 
to know people on a deeper level.

04:19.290 --> 04:21.300
Akiyama-san, am I...

04:21.300 --> 04:22.810
You should doubt people.

04:23.160 --> 04:27.680
Doubt, doubt some more, 
and look straight into their hearts.

04:28.230 --> 04:33.000
The more painful someone's truth, 
the more reluctant they are to speak it.

04:35.270 --> 04:36.200
All right.

04:39.030 --> 04:41.580
Then, the next morning...

04:42.610 --> 04:45.100
Ms. Nao Kanzaki?

04:45.800 --> 04:47.200
For you.

04:47.200 --> 04:49.000
R-Right...

04:49.000 --> 04:53.910
You'll be using that card in the game,
 so be sure to hold on to it.

04:50.100 --> 04:54.600
Nao Kanzaki

04:54.900 --> 05:01.080
Now, everyone, I'll take you to the venue
 for the Liar Game's third round.

05:09.480 --> 05:13.950
Wait, is the venue for the 
third round gonna be...

05:13.950 --> 05:16.050
Indeed. It is the airport.

05:16.050 --> 05:18.540
Huh?! Why the airport?!

05:18.540 --> 05:22.220
Are they gonna fly us outta the country?!

05:22.550 --> 05:23.860
Don't be stupid.

05:23.860 --> 05:26.000
We don't even have passports.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.370
You don't know that!

05:27.370 --> 05:31.680
A shady organization like this might 
have ways to smuggle people overseas!

05:31.680 --> 05:34.440
I-I'm sure that's not what this is!

05:34.440 --> 05:36.680
Hey, what's the deal?!

05:38.060 --> 05:41.170
You've come to a very apt conclusion.

05:42.020 --> 05:47.820
Because the third-round game is about 
traveling between two different countries.

05:55.820 --> 05:57.700
This is the venue.

05:57.700 --> 06:02.740
Until recently, it was used 
as an immigration checkpoint.

06:03.330 --> 06:07.330
Now it is a mere shell of itself,
 soon to be torn down.

06:07.660 --> 06:10.680
They can rent out a place 
like this for a game?

06:10.680 --> 06:13.150
Just how big is this organization?

06:16.160 --> 06:18.250
A fine day to you all!

06:18.250 --> 06:22.970
It is truly a pleasure to see you again.

06:23.560 --> 06:27.680
Now, allow me to explain the game 
you'll be playing this round.

06:27.680 --> 06:31.810
It differs from the prior games 
in that it is a team competition.

06:31.810 --> 06:32.990
A team competition?

06:33.500 --> 06:35.340
We're on teams?

06:35.340 --> 06:36.800
Who's on whose side?

06:37.240 --> 06:41.000
Now, the game we'll 
be playing is called...

06:41.280 --> 06:42.750
the Contraband Game!

06:42.750 --> 06:45.550
Contraband Game?

06:45.550 --> 06:50.370
I knew it! You're taking us overseas 
to be criminal accessories!

06:50.370 --> 06:51.880
Certainly not.

06:51.880 --> 06:54.870
The contraband is in the game only.

06:54.870 --> 06:57.150
You will not be doing anything illegal.

06:57.460 --> 07:02.030
Of course, "contraband" does suggest 
smuggling between countries.

07:02.030 --> 07:05.270
Thus we have prepared 
make-believe foreign countries.

07:05.570 --> 07:07.770
Look out the window.

07:08.770 --> 07:10.560
That's a foreign country?

07:10.560 --> 07:11.930
Correct.

07:11.930 --> 07:14.010
This room is the Country of Day.

07:14.010 --> 07:16.360
That room is the Country of Night.

07:16.360 --> 07:18.790
From your perspective, a foreign land.

07:19.080 --> 07:21.040
Oh, so that's all?

07:21.380 --> 07:25.540
Allow me to tell you more
 about these two countries.

07:25.540 --> 07:43.560
Country of Day

07:25.540 --> 07:43.560
Country of Night

07:25.910 --> 07:30.020
Relations between the Country of Day and
the Country of Night have soured of late.

07:30.020 --> 07:34.440
In 72 hours, a war will 
break out between them.

07:34.950 --> 07:37.050
This is a problem for you,

07:37.050 --> 07:39.770
because you are international traders.

07:39.770 --> 07:43.560
You have a great deal of funds
in the other country.

07:43.920 --> 07:48.060
When the war breaks out, 
what will happen to that capital?

07:48.320 --> 07:50.920
Well, it's enemy money.

07:50.920 --> 07:52.820
They'll probably seize it.

07:52.820 --> 07:54.600
Correct.

07:54.600 --> 07:56.580
Therefore, before the war starts...

07:56.580 --> 08:05.960
Country of Day

07:56.580 --> 08:05.960
Country of Night

07:56.580 --> 08:05.960
Third Country

07:56.580 --> 08:01.940
You want to retrieve as much of your 
money from that country as possible

08:01.940 --> 08:05.540
and evacuate it to a safe third country.

08:07.260 --> 08:09.720
Um, what's this "third country"?

08:10.020 --> 08:16.590
Imagine a bank in a perpetually 
neutral country, like Switzerland.

08:16.950 --> 08:20.040
But as is the case 
throughout modern society,

08:20.040 --> 08:24.100
it is illegal to move large amounts of 
cash across borders without permission.

08:24.420 --> 08:29.190
At the border, you'll face a formidable 
inspector hoping to confiscate it.

08:29.190 --> 08:32.980
Thus, you must get the cash across
the border while evading discovery.

08:33.260 --> 08:37.120
I see. So we're smuggling 
contraband cash.

08:37.500 --> 08:39.600
Let us try it in practice.

08:39.600 --> 08:42.100
The four of you will be 
the Country of Day team.

08:42.100 --> 08:45.120
You five will be the 
Country of Night team.

08:45.120 --> 08:47.500
You've picked our teams already?!

08:47.500 --> 08:51.150
No, this is a practice run, nothing more.

08:51.150 --> 08:52.900
You may listen without fear.

08:53.600 --> 08:57.700
Teams will take turns 
on offense and defense.

08:58.160 --> 09:00.540
When the Country of Day 
is smuggling contraband cash,

09:00.540 --> 09:02.600
the Country of Night will 
serve as inspectors.

09:02.600 --> 09:04.740
When the turn is over,
 the teams will swap.

09:04.740 --> 09:09.770
The Country of Night will then smuggle,
and the Country of Day will inspect.

09:10.010 --> 09:13.340
Let us play one turn with the 
Country of Day on offense.

09:13.340 --> 09:16.590
First, nominate one person from 
your team to be your smuggler.

09:16.990 --> 09:19.040
Anyone may volunteer.

09:20.980 --> 09:23.410
Then I'll give it a try.

09:23.730 --> 09:25.980
The player chosen as the smuggler

09:25.980 --> 09:28.960
will enter the other country 
through the border crossing gate.

09:29.620 --> 09:32.390
Let us all go there together.

09:33.280 --> 09:37.920
First, you will leave the Country of Day 
lobby and move down the corridor.

09:38.170 --> 09:39.930
There, you will find an elevator.

09:40.320 --> 09:44.670
You will take the elevator 
one floor up and follow the hall.

09:47.300 --> 09:48.810
It's a border!

09:48.810 --> 09:54.810
Yes, this is the border between the 
Country of Day and the Country of Night.

09:55.190 --> 09:58.320
You will cross the border 
and continue onward,

09:58.610 --> 10:00.810
where you will find a cash dispenser.

10:00.810 --> 10:02.950
This is the Country of Night Bank.

10:04.690 --> 10:09.560
It contains a great deal of money 
belonging to Country of Day players.

10:10.460 --> 10:16.720
On the opposite side of the border 
you crossed is the Country of Day Bank.

10:17.220 --> 10:22.060
It contains a great deal of money 
belonging to Country of Night players.

10:23.590 --> 10:25.460
Smugglers from both countries

10:25.460 --> 10:28.170
will attempt to withdraw money 
from the foreign ATM,

10:28.170 --> 10:31.740
put it in a suitcase, 
and return it to their country.

10:32.160 --> 10:35.230
Um, how do we withdraw the money?

10:35.530 --> 10:38.000
This functions exactly like a normal ATM.

10:38.000 --> 10:40.720
You were given a card 
at the bowling alley, yes?

10:40.720 --> 10:43.750
Oh, that's right.

10:43.750 --> 10:46.500
Insert your card into the machine.

10:46.500 --> 10:48.370
O-Okay...

10:49.020 --> 10:54.700
When you insert your card, 
it will display your current balance.

10:55.290 --> 10:57.970
One, ten...

10:57.960 --> 11:00.970
Balance

10:58.710 --> 11:00.970
Th-Th...

11:00.970 --> 11:03.560
Three hundred million?!

11:03.560 --> 11:04.780
Correct.

11:04.780 --> 11:08.600
You hold 300 million yen 
in the Country of Night Bank.

11:08.600 --> 11:10.320
That's so much!

11:10.320 --> 11:12.480
But wait, there's more!

11:12.480 --> 11:14.770
The funds you once held 
in your own country

11:14.770 --> 11:17.500
have already been evacuated 
to the third country.

11:17.500 --> 11:19.120
You have 100 million there.

11:19.120 --> 11:25.990
In other words, you have a total 
of 400 million in this game.

11:26.310 --> 11:29.680
What was once 100 million 
has become 400 million.

11:29.680 --> 11:33.740
In other words, your opportunity
 has quadrupled.

11:37.540 --> 11:39.450
Everyone present knew...

11:39.450 --> 11:46.340
that quadruple the funds
 also meant quadruple the risk.

11:50.840 --> 11:54.170
The smuggler will withdraw money
 and take it with them.

11:54.170 --> 11:58.000
Only money within the briefcase counts.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.690
You may take any amount that you wish.

12:01.040 --> 12:02.940
Fifty million, one million...

12:02.940 --> 12:04.590
Even zero, if you so choose.

12:04.590 --> 12:09.830
However, the briefcase can only 
hold 100 million at a time.

12:09.830 --> 12:12.090
A hundred million in cash?!

12:12.090 --> 12:14.660
Correct. Would you like to see?

12:19.830 --> 12:22.230
I-It's all real...

12:23.430 --> 12:25.040
Now, Kanzaki-san,

12:25.040 --> 12:27.480
withdraw as much as you'd like.

12:27.480 --> 12:28.480
Okay...

12:37.530 --> 12:38.870
I've made my withdrawal.

12:39.600 --> 12:41.880
You will now transport 
your contraband cash.

12:42.600 --> 12:47.680
Proceed down the Country of Night hall, 
take the elevator to the floor below,

12:47.680 --> 12:51.380
and continue until you 
reach the border again.

12:53.030 --> 12:54.770
This is the inspection room.

12:55.120 --> 12:57.500
This man will always be here.

12:57.500 --> 13:00.340
He is a member of the airport 
police known as a checker.

13:02.390 --> 13:05.240
The inspection room is fully soundproof.

13:05.240 --> 13:08.040
No one can hear what goes on within.

13:08.380 --> 13:11.600
Those inside also cannot hear
 what transpires outside.

13:12.220 --> 13:15.690
I can't see out through this window.

13:15.690 --> 13:17.410
It is one-way glass.

13:17.410 --> 13:20.020
You can see perfectly well 
from the other side.

13:20.350 --> 13:23.420
The smuggler, Kanzaki-san, will sit here.

13:23.420 --> 13:26.160
The inspector will sit across from her.

13:26.500 --> 13:30.900
Now, Country of Night players,
 choose someone to play your inspector.

13:31.460 --> 13:32.680
I'll do it.

13:33.800 --> 13:38.500
The smuggler and inspector 
will now be alone in this room.

13:38.500 --> 13:41.700
The inspector must identify
if the smuggler has contraband.

13:41.700 --> 13:44.300
They may ask questions, 
or they may simply observe.

13:44.590 --> 13:48.120
However, you may not touch the briefcase.

13:48.120 --> 13:50.080
You have ten minutes.

13:50.080 --> 13:53.600
Use that time to deduce whether 
or not they are carrying contraband.

13:53.600 --> 13:55.060
When finished, press this button

13:55.060 --> 13:57.520
to remove the soundproofing 
and make your declaration.

13:57.830 --> 14:00.470
If you think the briefcase 
is empty, say "pass."

14:00.470 --> 14:03.600
If you think the briefcase 
contains money, say "doubt."

14:04.110 --> 14:09.440
If you say "doubt," you must also declare 
how much money you think the player has.

14:09.990 --> 14:13.320
If you think they are carrying one 
million, say "doubt one million."

14:11.660 --> 14:13.950
Doubt 1 million

14:13.750 --> 14:17.170
If you think they are carrying 
50 million, say "doubt 50 million."

14:15.200 --> 14:17.790
Doubt 50 million

14:18.140 --> 14:21.860
However, if you declare "doubt" 
and the smuggler is innocent,

14:21.860 --> 14:25.460
the inspector must offer compensation—

14:25.460 --> 14:29.540
that is, pay damages to the smuggler 
from their third-country bank account.

14:29.540 --> 14:31.060
Pay damages?

14:31.310 --> 14:34.390
Damages are paid to the sum 
of half the accused declaration.

14:34.390 --> 14:36.870
If they said "doubt one million," 
they must pay 500,000.

14:36.870 --> 14:40.050
If they said "doubt 50 million," 
they must pay 25 million.

14:40.360 --> 14:43.210
After the inspector declares 
either "doubt" or "pass,"

14:43.210 --> 14:46.220
the checker will come in and confirm 
the contents of the briefcase.

14:47.290 --> 14:50.060
Then comes the moment of truth!

14:50.660 --> 14:52.950
The inspector says "pass"

14:53.070 --> 14:55.450
Pass

14:53.160 --> 14:54.250
Pass!

14:54.250 --> 14:57.690
The inspector says "pass," and you 
succeed in smuggling your contraband.

14:55.450 --> 14:57.700
Result

14:55.450 --> 14:57.700
Contraband smuggling succeeds

14:58.030 --> 15:01.970
If you're carrying 100 million,
 then you've obtained 100 million.

15:01.970 --> 15:05.730
If the briefcase is empty, 
of course, you gain nothing.

15:06.840 --> 15:09.590
Inspector says "doubt," but the case is empty

15:09.720 --> 15:11.470
Doubt 50 million

15:09.900 --> 15:11.660
Doubt 50 million!

15:11.660 --> 15:13.300
The briefcase is empty.

15:13.340 --> 15:16.850
Result

15:13.340 --> 15:16.850
Inspector pays damages to the smuggler

15:13.580 --> 15:16.850
But because the inspector 
falsely accused you

15:17.120 --> 15:22.720
and declared a doubt of 50 million,
they must pay half of that in damages.

15:23.400 --> 15:26.230
Inspector says "doubt," and the smuggler has the declared amount or less

15:26.360 --> 15:28.280
Doubt 50 million

15:26.450 --> 15:28.130
Doubt 50 million!

15:28.590 --> 15:30.480
There is 20 million inside.

15:30.480 --> 15:34.250
If the inspector declares "doubt" for 
more than the amount being carried,

15:30.490 --> 15:34.240
Result

15:30.490 --> 15:34.240
Contraband smuggling fails

15:34.250 --> 15:38.490
the inspector can seize the entire 
contents of the briefcase.

15:39.160 --> 15:41.620
Inspector says "doubt," and the smuggler has more than the amount declared

15:41.750 --> 15:43.670
Doubt 50 million

15:41.840 --> 15:43.640
Doubt 50 million!

15:44.060 --> 15:45.880
There is 60 million inside.

15:45.880 --> 15:50.130
Result

15:45.880 --> 15:50.130
Contraband smuggling succeeds
and inspector pays damages to the smuggler

15:45.880 --> 15:50.120
If the smuggler is carrying more than 
the amount declared, they succeed.

15:50.120 --> 15:54.040
In this case, the smuggler receives 
both their 60 million in contraband cash

15:53.640 --> 16:02.140
Contraband Cash

15:53.640 --> 16:02.140
60 million

15:54.040 --> 15:58.440
and half of the declared 50 million doubt,
25 million, in damages.

15:57.640 --> 16:02.140
Compensation

15:57.640 --> 16:02.140
25 million

15:58.440 --> 16:02.140
A total of 85 million.

15:59.220 --> 16:02.140
Total

15:59.220 --> 16:02.140
85 million

16:03.300 --> 16:07.220
For the inspector, 
Case 4 is adding insult to injury.

16:07.650 --> 16:09.260
Now, Akiyama-san,

16:09.260 --> 16:11.290
proceed with your inspection.

16:11.290 --> 16:13.520
You have ten minutes.

16:13.520 --> 16:15.510
I don't need ten minutes.

16:16.730 --> 16:18.090
Doubt one million.

16:19.040 --> 16:20.230
Checker.

16:25.830 --> 16:27.830
It's exactly one million!

16:27.830 --> 16:31.090
Well done. How did you know?

16:31.090 --> 16:32.650
It was simple.

16:32.650 --> 16:36.610
Each time she moved the briefcase, 
I could hear the money rattling around.

16:36.610 --> 16:40.490
I could tell from the sound it made 
that there was one bundle of bills inside.

16:41.700 --> 16:45.530
Magnificent. 
The inspector wins this exchange.

16:45.530 --> 16:49.530
This one million yen will go into 
Akiyama-san's third-country bank account,

16:49.530 --> 16:54.480
and the loser, Kanzaki-san, has lost that
 money from her Country of Night account.

16:54.750 --> 16:56.980
The teams will now switch sides.

16:56.980 --> 16:59.120
The Country of Night 
will take a turn smuggling,

16:59.120 --> 17:02.790
and the Country of Day will play 
the inspector trying to stop them.

17:03.490 --> 17:06.110
One turn on each side 
constitutes a full round.

17:06.110 --> 17:08.620
We will play fifty rounds.

17:08.620 --> 17:10.140
Fifty rounds?!

17:10.140 --> 17:11.120
That'll take forever!

17:11.120 --> 17:13.520
Far from it.

17:13.520 --> 17:15.710
You will see once you begin,

17:15.710 --> 17:17.840
but fifty rounds will pass swiftly,

17:17.840 --> 17:20.470
as if in the blink of an eye.

17:20.790 --> 17:25.820
Use that limited time to transfer as much
cash as you can from the other country

17:25.820 --> 17:27.910
and into your third-country accounts.

17:28.680 --> 17:30.950
The moment the fifty rounds
 have concluded,

17:30.950 --> 17:35.890
the team with more money in their 
third-country accounts will be the winner.

17:36.490 --> 17:39.590
And regarding individual prize money,

17:39.590 --> 17:41.810
regardless of victory 
or defeat for your team,

17:41.810 --> 17:46.130
the entire amount in your third-country 
account will serve as your prize.

17:46.130 --> 17:47.370
The entire amount...

17:47.370 --> 17:48.510
...will be...

17:48.780 --> 17:49.990
...our prize?

17:50.250 --> 17:55.070
For instance, if you succeed in 
smuggling your entire 300 million,

17:55.070 --> 17:57.610
so you end with 400 million 
in your third-country account,

17:57.610 --> 18:01.070
that amount in full will be yours.

18:01.690 --> 18:05.760
Contraband is not the only way to 
increase the money in your account.

18:06.080 --> 18:11.270
If you can get an inspector to pay you
 damages, that money also belongs to you.

18:07.350 --> 18:11.270
+Paid Compensation 200 million yen

18:11.270 --> 18:13.770
Awesome! Another 200 mil for me!

18:14.100 --> 18:17.780
And if, as an inspector, you prevent 
your opponent from smuggling,

18:17.780 --> 18:19.780
the money they're carrying becomes yours.

18:19.780 --> 18:23.550
Awesome! I seized 100 million 
in contraband cash five times!

18:23.160 --> 18:25.160
+500 million yen

18:23.550 --> 18:25.170
That's 500 mil more for me!

18:25.170 --> 18:29.330
If you fail to smuggle all of your money 
after the conclusion of fifty rounds,

18:29.330 --> 18:33.170
any remaining funds are confiscated 
by the country in which they were left.

18:33.170 --> 18:36.910
For instance, if the members 
of the Country of Night

18:36.910 --> 18:41.690
leave a total of 400 million 
in the Country of Day,

18:41.690 --> 18:45.060
that 400 million will be distributed 
equally among the Country of Day players.

18:45.500 --> 18:49.950
Well? This prize is incomparable 
to those in the first two games!

18:50.380 --> 18:54.190
It's your big chance to earn
 even a billion yen!

18:54.480 --> 19:00.340
But the 400 million we've lent you for the
game must be returned when it is over.

19:01.440 --> 19:02.700
Excuse me.

19:03.000 --> 19:05.780
You've left out one crucial detail.

19:05.780 --> 19:08.080
How are the teams being divided?

19:09.210 --> 19:12.830
I mean, this is all about 
who you work with, right?

19:12.830 --> 19:16.070
We've got some smart cookies 
and some real dum-dums here.

19:16.070 --> 19:19.720
I'm not gonna be happy 
if the teams aren't fair.

19:19.720 --> 19:23.600
As a matter of fact, 
that has already been determined.

19:23.600 --> 19:25.900
Then tell us our teams already!

19:26.120 --> 19:29.270
Now, now. I'm about to do so.

19:29.620 --> 19:33.020
I will begin with the Country of Day team.

19:33.020 --> 19:39.400
Please, let me be with Akiyama-san!
Let me be with Akiyama-san!

19:40.130 --> 19:42.260
The Country of Day team will consist of...

19:43.390 --> 19:46.160
all nine people here!

19:47.160 --> 19:50.410
Yay! I'm with you, Akiyama-san!

19:50.410 --> 19:52.700
W-Wait a minute!

19:52.700 --> 19:54.420
If we're all the Country of Day team,

19:54.420 --> 19:56.710
then who's the Country of Night?!

19:57.940 --> 20:00.050
Step out and meet them.

20:01.470 --> 20:04.300
These nine people make up
 the Country of Night.

20:04.610 --> 20:08.300
They will be your opponents 
in this game.

20:14.180 --> 20:15.440
Well, then...

20:15.440 --> 20:20.900
In one hour, the Liar Game's third round, 
the Contraband Game, shall begin!

20:20.900 --> 20:22.070
Wh-Who are you?

20:22.070 --> 20:23.830
I do beg your pardon.

20:23.830 --> 20:28.430
I will be serving as this game's 
dealer alongside Leronira.

20:28.430 --> 20:30.570
My name is Nearco.

20:30.570 --> 20:34.580
I urge you all to work together 
and seek victory!

20:36.650 --> 20:39.760
Let us meet again in an hour.

20:41.740 --> 20:45.900
Those Country of Night guys 
looked pretty tough.

20:45.900 --> 20:48.960
I can't believe we're going up 
against people like that.

20:50.950 --> 20:53.980
When I first heard Nao-chan's 
"surefire win" pitch,

20:53.980 --> 20:56.500
I really thought we'd be able 
to take on the world...

20:56.500 --> 20:58.540
I really thought we'd be able 
to take on the world...

20:59.130 --> 21:02.280
How are the Country of Day players?

21:02.730 --> 21:05.490
They are deceptively capable.

21:05.790 --> 21:10.990
Fukunaga here is exceptionally 
smart and physically strong,

21:11.320 --> 21:13.350
and most importantly, ruthless.

21:13.350 --> 21:16.380
Ruthless! How delightful.

21:16.380 --> 21:20.660
But there is someone who exceeds 
even Fukunaga in brains...

21:21.230 --> 21:23.290
This man, Akiyama.

21:23.930 --> 21:29.060
But they are not the ones who 
have most caught my attention.

21:29.350 --> 21:32.520
That would be this girl, Nao Kanzaki.

21:32.520 --> 21:34.690
I have heard the rumors.

21:34.690 --> 21:38.330
But she doesn't seem 
particularly cunning to me.

21:39.380 --> 21:42.690
She's not cunning in the slightest.

21:42.690 --> 21:44.680
She's as stupid as they come,

21:44.680 --> 21:47.580
and of a very different nature 
from the rest of the players.

21:48.000 --> 21:51.920
But her differences will, at times,

21:51.920 --> 21:55.250
afford her unexpected strength.

21:55.250 --> 21:56.660
I see.

21:57.430 --> 21:58.570
However...

21:58.880 --> 22:01.920
Your team is surely insurmountable.

22:01.920 --> 22:05.470
Given its formidable linchpin, Yokoya.

22:07.210 --> 22:09.370
Yokoya, you say?

22:09.370 --> 22:12.540
Yokoya is indeed someone to be feared.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.020
Next Time

23:45.020 --> 23:50.020
Yokoya
